@startuml state-machine
title MotionPlanner - avoidance manoeuvre (what the 10-step plan contains)

[*] --> Disarmed : boot

Disarmed : no plan published
Cruise : 10 cruise steps
Stop : zero power, stop_duration_s
Reverse : reverse_speed, reverse_duration_s
Turn : spin counter-clockwise, turn_duration_s
Fault : plan of zeros

Disarmed --> Cruise : frame.armed
Cruise --> Stop : range < stop_distance_cm
Stop --> Reverse : after stop_duration_s
Reverse --> Turn : after reverse_duration_s
Turn --> Cruise : after turn_duration_s

Cruise --> Fault : range invalid or\nframe older than frame_stale_ms
Fault --> Cruise : valid fresh frame

Cruise --> Disarmed : not frame.armed
Stop --> Disarmed : not frame.armed
Reverse --> Disarmed : not frame.armed
Turn --> Disarmed : not frame.armed

note right of Turn
  Stop, Reverse and Turn are one committed manoeuvre.
  The planner keeps to it on every replan,
  whatever the range says, until it ends.
end note

note bottom of Cruise
  The controller applies its own limits on top
  (hard stop, blind stop, plan heartbeat), whatever the plan says.
end note

@enduml
